# Run outputs under any name. The list above names specific default paths and
# so caught nothing when a run was given --review-file or --report-file, which
# is how six untracked c15_b5/c15_b20 files from the batch-size experiment
# accumulated in data/. The findings from those runs live in the fix log; the
# raw output is reproducible and is not worth versioning.
data/*_review.jsonl
data/*_rejected.jsonl
data/*_report.json
data/*_sample.tsv
data/translation_backfill_report.json

# The translation store, NOT a golden fixture despite living under
# data/fixtures/. It is a 35 MB operational cache of every Azure translation
# ever made (about 200,000 lines), grown a bit at a time against a monthly
# free-tier allowance. Committing it would put a large binary-ish blob in
# history for no review value; losing it would cost weeks of free tier to
# rebuild. So: never committed, never deleted. Section 7's "golden fixtures
# are versioned in data/fixtures/" still holds for every other path there.
# The location is a misnomer inherited from build_translations.py's default
# and is deliberately not being moved right now; a move would break the store
# on the owner's machine for no benefit.
data/fixtures/translations/

# Billing exports pulled from the owner's Google Cloud account, read by
# scripts/reconcile_cost_log.py and scripts/repair_cost_log.py. Personal
# financial records. They belong on the operator's disk, never in the repo,
# and least of all in a repo that may go public.
data/cost/

# Git bundles used to hand work between the agent's sandbox and the owner's
# machine. Pure transport. Once fetched, the commits are in history and the
# file is dead weight; before being fetched it is the only copy, which is why
# they are ignored rather than deleted by tooling.
*.bundle

# Scratch copies made while CLAUDE.md was still gitignored.
CLAUDE.md.new
*_tmp.tsv

